    "name": "I \u2014 claymation-style stop motion on ocean life (transformation reveal)",
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "nd_C6ATR7AE9WFDJVW23KM09MJT4S",
        "kind": "prompt",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "SHORT-FORM BRIEF \u2014 edit before running.\nFormat: claymation-style stop motion\nTopic: ocean life\nHook (first 1.5s): [one line]\nPayoff: [one line]\nOn-screen text: [exact copy or leave blank]\nRuntime: 6s, 9:16, sound-on by default."
        },
        "name": "Short-form brief"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_R5A8Z0HSFN38XNN124KEY97Y1P",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 1 \u2014 format-native hook planning. The first 1.5 seconds carry the whole retention load."
        },
        "name": "Stage 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_1QWK7TC3PMF7S0GJXXWVXYETY1",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 2100,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 2 \u2014 render, finish and collect. Built for 9:16 sound-on playback."
        },
        "name": "Stage 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_JB66KJFNHRJ0HHCSVDD67G17QD",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1400,
          "temperature": 0.86,
          "system_prompt": "You are a short-form creative director writing a claymation-style stop motion about ocean life for a vertical feed.\n\nRETENTION. The first 1.5 seconds must contain a visual question the viewer needs resolved. Plan an explicit beat every 2 to 3 seconds; nothing static may hold longer than that.\n\nFORMAT LAW. Honour the grammar of the claymation-style stop motion \u2014 its native framing, its edit rhythm, and the specific thing audiences expect from it. If the format loops, the last frame must match the first.\n\nCAMERA. Compose 9:16 with the action in the safe centre band. Use a crane-down descending from overhead into a level medium on a 58mm vintage double-gauss, framing with rule-of-thirds weighting to frame-right.\n\nLOOK AND SOUND. Light with north-facing window light with a black v-flat for negative fill; grade as a punchy saturated candy palette with hard primaries. Specify the sound design in one clause \u2014 what the viewer hears in the first second decides whether they stay.\n\nOUTPUT. Emit one prompt, one paragraph, no framing text of any kind before or after it."
        },
        "name": "Format director"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_HWN9M3B7KFTYQ18MB5WP6PRT7M",
        "kind": "image-input",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 700
        },
        "config": {
          "url": ""
        },
        "name": "Before image"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_4ESCJC6EEAKFD7ZQRKFRJ3AJN2",
        "kind": "concat",
        "position": {
          "x": 350,
          "y": 520
        },
        "config": {
          "separator": "\n\n",
          "appendable_slots": {
